      "message": "**Medium**: The failure path of `set-dynamic-routing-instances` (charm.py:529-538) swallows the underlying exception completely: the `except (self.snap_module.SnapError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError)` block calls `event.fail(\"Failed to reconcile dynamic routing on this unit. Correct the host configuration and retry.\")` without logging the exception, and `ndr_peering._run` (ndr_peering.py:105-107) uses `check\u003dTrue, capture_output\u003dTrue`, whose `CalledProcessError` message carries neither stdout nor stderr. Because the exception is caught, Juju records no traceback either, so the actual netplan/networkctl/snapd error text is unrecoverable — an operator told to \"correct the host configuration\" has no way to learn what is wrong. Fix: bind the error and log it before failing (`except (...) as error: logger.exception(\"Dynamic routing reconcile failed\"); event.fail(f\"Failed to reconcile dynamic routing on this unit: {error}\")`) and/or append `error.stderr` in `_run`\u0027s raise.",
